      "writtenOn": "2019-03-11T16:21:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Currently, BATTERY_LEVEL_SHUTDOWN can be changed by redefining it in board.h. If it\u0027s not redefined, the default value is used. With this change, the same rule applies. board_set_battery_level_shutdown can be redefined in board.c. If not, the default function will be used.\n\nWhen there is a default value or behavior, I believe this is the simplest implementation in C. I don\u0027t see a particular problem with renaming or refactoring.",
